---
title: Vegan Thai Green Curry Tofu
portions: 4
category: Thai
source: "https://cinnamonsnail.com/vegan-green-curry-tofu/"
---

## Tofu

[Press] Press the @tofu{400 g} and cut it into bite-sized pieces.

[Fry] Heat @vegetable-oil{45 ml} in a #pot{} over medium-high heat. Fry the tofu until golden and crisp, ~{8 min}. Transfer to a plate. ->&crispy tofu{}

## Curry

[Sauté] In the same #pot{}, heat the remaining @vegetable-oil{20 ml} over medium heat. Sauté the @shallot{75 g}, the @red-bell-pepper{150 g}, the @green-bell-pepper{150 g}, the @green-beans{200 g} and the @baby-corn{150 g} until softened, ~{5 min}.

[Bloom] Stir in the @green-curry-paste{45 g} and cook until fragrant, ~{2 min}.

[Season] Add the @brown-sugar{16 g}, the @lime-juice{20 ml}, the @salt{3 g} and the @water{120 ml}.

[Simmer] Pour in the @coconut-milk{400 ml}, return the &crispy tofu{} and bring to a gentle simmer for ~{5 min}.

[Finish] Stir in the @thai-basil{15 g} until wilted, ~{1 min}. Serve over @jasmine-rice{300 g}(cooked).
